{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact RC-1 head b8ebe87816d918c778e2378c834d4af06c46653a on builder/rc1-refusal-classes-20261113, all 9 artifacts, for request b0fe0668 under promise e9b0b075 and review request dfd0d08d. `REFUSAL_CLASSES` gives each of the 36 refusal reasons one class, and each `never` row holds at its judge site at the head.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- The table (`packages/bytes/src/records.ts:79-98`). It covers each key of `REFUSAL_REASONS` once: 6 `never`, 5 `protocol` and 25 `head`. `packages/bytes/src/index.ts:7` exports it.\n- A `never` row is the costly mistake: a client that reads `never` gives up for good. A `head` row that later proves final only costs retries until `notAfter`. So I checked each `never` row against its judge site:\n  - `floor-back`, `floor-ahead` and `floor-keep` (`floor.ts:164-173`). `floor-ahead` reads only the input. `floor-keep` reads the input and `own(seq)`. A position below the floor that the kept set lacks never comes back, because a keep list names only held positions and `archivedPosition` (`floor.ts:25-29`) reads the floor alone.\n  - `archived` (`operand.ts:371`) rests on the same `archivedPosition` rule.\n  - `scope-refused` (`judge.ts:243`, `delivery.ts:168`, `prepare.ts:221`, `settle.ts:42`). The only path past `delivery.ts:168` is a control message (`delivery.ts:166`). `confirmation` (`delivery.ts:318-327`) writes `activate` only when the status is `provisional`. A refused scope therefore stays refused.\n  - `late` (`delivery.ts:267`) is a recorded decision. `decided` (`delivery.ts:158`) answers a later copy with `repeat`.\n- The `protocol` rows. `unknown-act` (`judge.ts:246`) reads `declared.acts` of the scope's pinned definition, and no effect changes that definition. A client that names an unknown act disagrees with the scope's definition, as the class says.\n- The report states the counterexamples (`revision-moved`, `final`, `expired`) and the order in which `expired` runs before `scope-refused` and `archive